      "title": "How to read this",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 7
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "Temporary Gaugely probe, remove after use. Each block below has a variable at the top of the dashboard. **Check 1:** can you open the picker and does it list values? **Check 2:** after you pick values, does the text show them and does the count change? A literal `${...}` in the text means the app did not substitute that variable. `no rows` means the query ran and matched nothing."
